            "review_title": "Review at Gogi House",
            "review_text": "L T C\nSingapore, Singapore64 contributions\n0\nJapanese Food\nMar 2017\nWe had our lunch here at the Japanese food section. My Friend ordered grilled Saba fish, my Wife had the Kanpachi grilled cheek and I have stir-fried chicken bento set. We also salmon belly sashimi and 2 fruit tea drinks. The seafood very fresh and cooked to the right texture. Freshness is the standard hallmark for Japanese food. In Singapore many times we don't have that standard. Like miso soup so tasteful and fluid. Most of Singapore restaurants served very salty miso soup unless you are served by authenticated Japanese tradition. Strongly recommend if you are in Halong Vietnam The Korean BBQ next door also owned by same owners, served Korean style buffet meal. Some of my group went there. Good value. For us total bill was 1million dongs or S$90. for three of us. Good food great value. Bon appetite.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten March 28, 2017",
